	<key>readme</key>
	<string>## App Launcher

Type `app` (configurable) followed by a space and part of an app's name. Press ↩ to open it.

| Key | Action |
| ↩ | Open the app |
| ⌘↩ | Reveal in Finder |
| ⌘C | Copy the app's path |
| → | Alfred file actions |

Apps are found by walking the app folders directly, not through Spotlight, so this works even when Spotlight's index is broken. The searched folders are /Applications, ~/Applications, /System/Applications, the Safari cryptex and /System/Library/CoreServices/Applications. Up to three levels of subfolders are searched, including symlinked folders such as Nix Apps. Finder is also included.

The index is cached and rebuilt automatically whenever one of those folders changes (an app is installed, removed or renamed), and at least once a day.</string>
